1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,472
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,472 --> 00:00:04,945
Episode 38.

3
00:00:04,945 --> 00:00:07,934
Pip Follows the Wrong Instructions.

4
00:00:07,934 --> 00:00:10,828
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,828 --> 00:00:14,565
Why did Pip miss the star on the first attempt?

6
00:00:14,565 --> 00:00:16,086
Ready?

7
00:00:16,086 --> 00:00:18,192
Let us find out.

8
00:00:18,192 --> 00:00:21,847
Maya draws a grid on a large sheet of paper.

9
00:00:21,847 --> 00:00:24,741
A star marks the destination.

10
00:00:24,741 --> 00:00:28,084
Pip will follow a short program to reach it.

11
00:00:28,084 --> 00:00:31,548
Leo writes: Move forward two squares.

12
00:00:31,548 --> 00:00:33,369
Turn right.

13
00:00:33,369 --> 00:00:36,059
Move forward one square.

14
00:00:36,059 --> 00:00:40,842
Pip follows the instructions and arrives beside a picture of a banana.

15
00:00:40,842 --> 00:00:43,980
That is not the star, Maya says.

16
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,317
Pip checks his record.

17
00:00:46,317 --> 00:00:49,035
I followed every instruction.

18
00:00:49,035 --> 00:00:52,065
They examine the starting position.

19
00:00:52,065 --> 00:00:57,432
Leo imagined Pip facing the top of the page, but Pip was facing left.

20
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:02,010
We forgot to specify the starting direction, Maya realizes.

21
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:05,407
They add it and run the same sequence again.

22
00:01:05,407 --> 00:01:08,573
This time, Pip reaches the star.

23
00:01:08,573 --> 00:01:11,929
Next, Leo writes a longer program.

24
00:01:11,929 --> 00:01:16,195
One turn is wrong, so Pip ends up at the banana again.

25
00:01:16,195 --> 00:01:20,081
The banana is very popular today, says Pip.

26
00:01:20,081 --> 00:01:25,570
Instead of rewriting everything at random, the children trace each step with a finger.

27
00:01:25,570 --> 00:01:28,845
They find the incorrect turn and change it.

28
00:01:28,845 --> 00:01:34,592
That process of finding and fixing problems is called debugging, Ms. Park explains.

29
00:01:34,592 --> 00:01:40,230
Maya asks whether a computer always understands what a person really intends.

30
00:01:40,230 --> 00:01:45,624
It carries out the operations its system is built to perform, says Ms. Park.

31
00:01:45,624 --> 00:01:49,442
Clear instructions and checking results still matter.

32
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:52,309
Pip completes the route at last.

33
00:01:52,309 --> 00:01:56,766
He requests one final instruction: Celebrate politely.

34
00:01:56,766 --> 00:02:00,733
Leo writes it more precisely: Ring your bell once.

35
00:02:00,733 --> 00:02:02,839
Pip rings twice.

36
00:02:02,839 --> 00:02:05,027
Everyone looks at him.

37
00:02:05,027 --> 00:02:07,364
A joke, he says.

38
00:02:07,364 --> 00:02:10,652
Please do not debug my sense of humor.

39
00:02:10,652 --> 00:02:13,668
Now, a little more to discover.

40
00:02:13,668 --> 00:02:18,274
An algorithm is a sequence of steps for carrying out a task.

41
00:02:18,274 --> 00:02:21,915
The starting conditions can affect its result.

42
00:02:21,915 --> 00:02:26,413
Debugging means locating and correcting problems in a program.

43
00:02:26,413 --> 00:02:32,350
Tracing one step at a time helps connect what the instructions say with what actually happens.

44
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:35,380
Let us hear the main idea again.

45
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:39,877
The first route failed because the starting direction was unclear.

46
00:02:39,877 --> 00:02:43,614
A later route failed because one turn was wrong.

47
00:02:43,614 --> 00:02:48,220
The children checked the steps, found each problem, and corrected it.

48
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:51,222
Here are three useful expressions.

49
00:02:51,222 --> 00:02:54,266
You can listen, or say them with me.

50
00:02:54,266 --> 00:02:56,644
Which way are you facing?

51
00:02:56,644 --> 00:02:59,021
Which way are you facing?

52
00:02:59,021 --> 00:03:01,739
Follow one step at a time.

53
00:03:01,739 --> 00:03:04,456
Follow one step at a time.

54
00:03:04,456 --> 00:03:07,255
Let us find where it went wrong.

55
00:03:07,255 --> 00:03:10,054
Let us find where it went wrong.

56
00:03:10,054 --> 00:03:12,921
Remember our listening question?

57
00:03:12,921 --> 00:03:16,657
Why did Pip miss the star on the first attempt?

58
00:03:16,657 --> 00:03:18,845
Here is the answer.

59
00:03:18,845 --> 00:03:26,005
The children had not specified the starting direction, so Pip began facing a different way from the one Leo imagined.

60
00:03:26,005 --> 00:03:29,796
And here is a question just for your imagination.

61
00:03:29,796 --> 00:03:35,502
Could you give someone precise instructions for drawing a simple shape without showing it to them?

62
00:03:35,502 --> 00:03:38,668
There is more than one possible answer.

63
00:03:38,668 --> 00:03:41,820
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
